# Block-max conjunction for top-K boolean queries whose include is an intersection of terms, Tantivy 0.26.1
# Base: tantivy 0.26.1 (crates.io) plus tantivy-0.26.1-phrase-pruning.patch and tantivy-0.26.1-bool-not-pruning.patch
# Two or more MUST term clauses that read frequencies (`a AND b`, `+a +b +c`), with no SHOULD clause, run
# block_max_conjunction: windows whose summed block maxima cannot beat the threshold are skipped without
# decoding, and a candidate stops being sought as soon as its partial score cannot beat it. With MUST_NOT
# clauses the exclusion set filters the callback, as for the bool-not patch.
# Apply after the bool-not patch with: git apply -p1 tantivy-0.26.1-and-block-max.patch

